;; Phase A4 — function-address witness.
;;
;; Covers IR_FunctionAddr in the LIVE arm of the program (A3's
;; call_return.gc only had it in dead arms to keep qemu-execute happy).
;; The let-bound lambda forces an IR_FunctionAddr emit at the let-binding
;; site; the (callee) call then jumps through the GOAL pointer.
;;
;; The arm64 emit pattern is ADRP + ADD imm12 + SUB offset_reg (the SUB
;; converts the absolute function-entry address to a GOAL pointer; in the
;; harness offset_reg is zero so the GOAL pointer equals the absolute
;; address). The arm64-aware ObjectGenerator fix-up writes the ADRP imm21
;; (page diff) and ADD imm12 (within-page byte offset) so the call lands
;; on the lambda's entry point. The lambda returns 142.

(defun fortytwo ()
  (let ((callee (lambda () 142)))
    (callee)))
